        "created_at": "2016-03-16T13:50:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey, all!</p><p>Just wanted to toss out a little hype for my 'home' convention--<a href=\"http://www4.wittenberg.edu/student_organizations/rpguild/conventions/wittcon/xiii/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">WittCon, hosted by the Wittenberg Role-Playing Guild, in Springfield, Ohio</a>.</p><p>WittCon XIII: Murphy's Law is this Saturday (March 19th) from 9am until midnight. &nbsp;Just a $5 entry fee gets you into a legion of tabletop, board, card, and roleplaying games, a fantastic raffle (provided by Bookery Fantasy of Fairborn, OH), a costume contest, and a pizza/pop dinner by Beavercreek Pizza Dive.</p><p>Currently scheduled events include D&amp;D (of various editions), Rogue Trader, Traveller, World of Darkness, Cold Steel Wardens, Toon, Paranoia, and even a live-action \"Orc and Pie\" dungeon (complete with real pie, should you survive the dungeon!).</p><p>Vendors include Bell Book and Comic (Dayton, OH), This Nerdy Home (Englewood, OH), Green's Geekery (Columbus, OH), and Art by Kytsora (Dayton, OH).</p><p>I'll be running an UnPub Protozone event during the first two sessions, with a number of local designers bringing prototypes ready for playtest. &nbsp;In addition, I'll be running&nbsp;<em>Cold Steel Wardens</em> events in the evening. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Hope to see you there!</p>",
